# Pole Progress

Angular 21 SPA for a single pole-dance studio. One studio = one Supabase project + one deploy.

## Stack

- Angular 21: standalone components, signals, `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`. No NgModules.
- Tailwind CSS for all styling. No component CSS files unless a utility class cannot express it.
- Supabase: Postgres with RLS, Auth, Storage, and RPCs. Schema changes go in `supabase/migrations/` only.
- Nx workspace. Run tasks with `npx nx <target> <project>` (for example `npx nx serve app`).

## Code

- Strict TypeScript. No `any`. Type public APIs and signal state explicitly.
- Functional reactive style: a private `signal` for state, public `computed` for derived values, `inject()` for dependencies.
- Standalone architecture. Feature UI lives in `libs/features/`. Shared auth, data, and Supabase clients live in `libs/core/`.
- Respect module boundaries in `eslint.config.mjs`. `@org/data` must not depend on `@org/auth`.
- Keep files small. Add a function, type, or component only when a second caller needs it.
- DB rows store storage paths. Resolve private media with signed URLs at read time.

## Responses & Execution

- **Global Context Rule**: Angular 21 (signals, OnPush), Tailwind CSS, and strict typing apply to all generated code automatically. Do not repeat these constraints in prompts.
- Write production-ready code: typed, OnPush, and consistent with the surrounding file.
- Prefer editing the existing file over a new abstraction.
- Run Nx for lint, test, and build. Do not invent npm scripts.